The NVIDIA driver uses initial-exec TLS in its glcore, which
normally prevents such library from dlopening, as initial-exec
uses fixed offsets from the thread pointer. On glibc, the ldso
allocates extra space ahead of time for such purposes (allowing
usage of initial-exec up until it runs out). Take the same
strategy here and alloc some extra bytes to allow a late static
TLS allocation.

-- q66

diff --git a/ldso/dynlink.c b/ldso/dynlink.c
index 65c3117..78f464c 100644
